THE RESIDUE — invisible errors no pool-structure gate could catch
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  invisible errors with exactly one exact-amount KEY   1 of 32 (3.125%)
  ... and dup_ref unset as well                        0

  B_id                        |B|  keys  rows     pool     top1   margin   dup  gold in top5  label
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  287742256750             54.25M     1     5        5   0.0007   0.0000  True         False  single-key

  value mis-attributed by the residue   54.25M
  gold key was in the recorded top-5    0 of 1

  One exact-amount key, taken, and wrong, with the right key carrying the same
  value from outside the candidate set. From inside the pool the row looks like
  an unambiguous single hit. Pool structure cannot see that.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERDICT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. Is the blindness predictable without labels?
     YES. 31 of 32 invisible errors (96.88%) sit in pools
     offering more than one exact-amount key, against a 7.387% base
     rate — 13.11x lift. The signal is there at decision time.

  2. What would it cost?
     2,136 rows escalated, 1,941 of them correct — 10.0 correct
     auto-closes given up per wrong posting caught. Coverage 90.224% -> 83.559%
     (-6.665 pts), precision 98.368% -> 98.966% (+0.598 pts).

     NOT REFUSED ON PRICE. At 11.1 points per point this is
     materially cheaper than the 31.4 the project refused. It still
     costs 6.665 points of coverage — 2,136 more rows into a queue
     someone works before a deadline. That is a capacity question, and this
     script does not answer it. What it can say is that the measurement does
     not rule the gate out.

  3. What the gate would not buy. Escalating these rows surfaces them for review;
     it does not resolve them. Where the correct key was never in the top-5,
     review is the only remedy anyway — 20 of 32 invisible errors are in
     that position.

